  "question": {
    "text": "If the earth suddenly shrinks to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>64</mn></mfrac><mi>th</mi></math> of its original volume with its mass remaining the same, the period of rotation of earth becomes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>24</mn><mi>x</mi></mfrac><mi>h</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is ________",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "16",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/23d4810c-7db9-4065-86ad-e70cad439265.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 214px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo></math> constant;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi><mi>&#969;</mi></math></p><p>From the conservation of angular momentum,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mi>M</mi><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mi>R</mi></mstyle><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mstyle><mn>16</mn></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Using&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#969;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></math>&nbsp;for each case along with the respective angular frequencies,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>16</mn><mn>1</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Using&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mo>,</mo></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></math>&nbsp;by comparing with the given time period in the question.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></blockquote>",
